{"step_index":123,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-10-18T09:02:05Z","input_tokens":2412,"cache_read_tokens":108619,"output_tokens":1417,"thinking":"Sandbox restrictions prevent outbound connections. The attempt to bypass this with `BypassSandbox: true` is for connection testing. The initial test used TCP, but WireGuard operates over UDP. The focus shifts to the WireGuard interface when the user clicks \"Activate\".\n\n\nThe WireGuard handshake status will be examined: a \"NO handshake\" or only sent bytes suggests a blocked UDP port 443. This is common with Jio in India due to QUIC/HTTP3 filtering. The observed configuration lacks an MTU setting; this is a likely cause of packet fragmentation, especially on Jio networks. Without an explicit MTU value, WireGuard defaults to 1420, while Jio connections often require a lower value.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_to_file","args":{"CodeContent":"\"[Interface]\\nPrivateKey = sFKSmjjwigiLNv/RTKNiHiszO38KF1DWgm2zgfU7SXQ=\\nAddress = 10.104.3.130/32\\nDNS = 1.1.1.1, 8.8.8.8\\nMTU = 1280\\n\\n[Peer]\\nPublicKey = Rn6w1t6actF9XC0bMIXxO25rf31uFqm2/n5sYyK1UzQ=\\nEndpoint = 147.135.37.178:443\\nAllowedIPs = 0.0.0.0/0, ::/0\\nPersistentKeepalive = 25\\n\"","Description":"\"Adding MTU = 1280 to fix packet fragmentation on Jio mobile tethering\"","Overwrite":"true","TargetFile":"\"C:\\\\Users\\\\renu5\\\\Desktop\\\\US-VPN.conf\"","toolAction":"\"Updating US-VPN config with MTU fix\"","toolSummary":"\"Fix MTU in US config\""}}]}
